%N A399731 Number of labeled point-determining (mating) graphs on 2n vertices in which every vertex has odd degree.
%C A399731 A point-determining (mating) graph is a graph in which distinct vertices have distinct open neighborhoods. A graph in which every vertex has odd degree necessarily has an even number of vertices.
%H A399731 I. M. Gessel and J. Li, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/0705.0042">Enumeration of Point-Determining Graphs</a>, arXiv:0705.0042 [math.CO], 2007-2009.
%F A399731 For n >= 1, a(n) = (2n)! * Sum_{lambda partition of 2n} (-1)^(2n-k) O(lambda)/z_lambda, where k is the number of parts of lambda, z_lambda = Product_{j>=1} j^m_j*m_j!, and m_j is the multiplicity of j in lambda. Here O(lambda) = 0 if all parts of lambda are even, and O(lambda) = 2^(binomial(k-1,2)) otherwise. Also, a(0) = 1.
%e A399731 a(2) = 4: the four labeled graphs on 4 vertices are the three perfect matchings and K_4.
%Y A399731 Cf. A006024 (labeled point-determining graphs), A122067 (labeled graphs in which every vertex has odd degree), A399730 (labeled Eulerian point-determining graphs).
%K A399731 nonn,new
